|~ `::snippet`, the kind of a snippet, and the laws declared under it.

   The rules it holds: [QSDSP#residence], [QSSLF#doc]. ~|

:snippet
  |~~ A snippet is a query a page shows its reader to run and see:
      written in the prose of a doc as a quote under this tag,
      ::snippet~(::vec | manifest) lists the verbs of vectors, and
      ::snippet~({:scores [5 6]} | get /scores/-1) shows a path read. `answer`
      runs it, and `snippets` reads the snippets of a doc.

      A snippet answers what its code answers, a failure among them; a
      link opens a page, and a law answers true.
      ::link~(::link) ::link~(::qlang/hypertext)
  ~~|
  ::kind
    | accepts
        |~~ The query a snippet shows, a quote, or a link, which the snippet
            makes a snippet as well.
        ~~|
        #[::quote ::link]
    | throws :PayloadKindNotTakenError
        |~~ A snippet holds the query a reader runs to see what it shows, a
            quote, or a link, `::snippet~(::vec | manifest)`; a quote under
            another tag gives the quote beneath by `payload`.
        ~~|
    | proves :answersWhatItShows
        |~~ A snippet answers what it shows. ~~|
        ~(|~~ ::snippet~(::vec | manifest) ~~| | snippets | first | answer
          | has ::vec/count)
    | proves :PayloadKindNotTakenError/refusesAString
        |~~ A snippet is a quote. ~~|
        ~(::snippet"x" !| tag | eq ::snippet/PayloadKindNotTakenError);

